cff-version: 1.2.0
title: eigenkit
message: >-
  If you use eigenkit in your research, please cite it using the metadata
  below.
type: software
authors:
  - name: EigenOrbit
    email: info@eigenorbit.com
    website: "https://eigenorbit.com"
repository-code: "https://github.com/eigenorbit/eigenkit"
url: "https://docs.kit.eigenorbit.com"
abstract: >-
  eigenkit puts one interface over many quantum backends. A circuit is written
  once as provider-neutral data, recompiled for each backend (PennyLane,
  Qiskit, Amazon Braket, IQM, CUDA-Q, TensorCircuit, Qulacs, qsim and a
  built-in numpy simulator), and returns the same values and gradients on all
  of them. Quantum machine learning, optimization (QAOA) and chemistry (VQE)
  sit on that one interface, with PyTorch layers and scikit-learn estimators.
keywords:
  - quantum computing
  - quantum machine learning
  - variational quantum circuits
  - QAOA
  - VQE
  - pytorch
  - scikit-learn
license: Apache-2.0
